  <work>
    <work-title>Hidden voices: a hymn, SATB on two staves</work-title>
  </work>
  <!-- Soprano (voice 1) and alto (voice 2) share the upper staff, tenor (5) and bass (6) the lower one, with the stems
       of each pair given (up, down). The lyrics are given with the soprano, as in hymnals; the last syllable of measure 1
       ("with") with the alto too.
       Measure 1, beat 3: the soprano's slurred eighths, the first in unison with the alto's quarter.
       Measure 2: only the soprano starts a note at beat 2 ("ces"), the alto holds a half note.
       Measure 3: the soprano's C sharp at beat 1, the alto's at beat 2 (without its own accidental); the alto rests at beat 1.
       Measure 4: a chord symbol at beat 2, where only the soprano starts a note. -->
